{"type":"text","text":"**Subject:** Venue update — Harbor Hall confirmed for March 12\n\nHi Dana,\n\nQuick update on the venue: Harbor Hall has confirmed us for March 12 — our original date. Priya also offered a walkthrough on March 3, which I think works on my end, but let me know if you have a conflict.\n\nThe final quote is $4,200, a bit under what we'd budgeted. They waived the AV setup fee since we're bringing our own projector. It covers up to 85 guests, which is right around our current RSVP count, so we should be fine barring a wave of late sign-ups.\n\nThey also sent a draft contract. I read through it and nothing stood out as unusual, but I'd like you to take a look before I sign. **Could you get me any comments by Friday?** If I don't hear back, I'll go ahead and send the signed copy.\n\nLet me know if you have questions or want to talk it through.\n\nThanks,\nSam\n\n---\n\n**What changed:**\n- Cut the length apology and throat-clearing — the update now leads with the news.\n- Made the subject line say something.\n- Broke the three topics (date, budget, contract) into clear paragraphs.\n- Turned the vague \"if I don't hear back\" into an actual deadline request, so Dana knows what's needed and by when.\n- Fixed the false reassurance: 85 guests vs. \"right around\" the current count isn't much cushion, so it now says \"barring a wave of late sign-ups.\""}
